{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966815,"nonce":"Xd9GiY+YDTbjzz466LPkziIZCNw=","title":"Ruffle 2D finish plan (post-M7)","message":"Goal: drain every ⏳ row in ROADMAP.md's 2D inventory tables\n(2D selection \u0026 transform · 2D vector authoring · 2D SDF\nprimitives · Fills, strokes, effects · Clipping/masking)\nbefore the editor moves to 3D authoring (M17). Phases are\nordered to land low-risk SDF + tool-completeness wins first,\nthen take on bigger surface (gradient gizmo, clip mask,\ncurve booleans). Each phase = one or more sub-milestones,\neach shippable on its own with a demo + tests.\n\nRound out the \"place a primitive\" tool family. Data variants\nalready exist (`ShapePath::RegularPolygon`, `ShapePath::Star`,\n`ShapePath::RoundedRect`); only the tool + on-canvas gizmos are\nmissing.\n\n- M7.10a — **Star / RegularPolygon place tool**\n  - `SdfPrimitiveTool` gains Star + Polygon kinds (alongside\n    Circle / Ellipse / RoundedRect).\n  - Press-drag radius from centre; release commits.\n  - Toolbar chip in `m7_sdf_tool` demo.\n  - Sides count: configurable per-tool (default star = 5,\n    polygon = 6); `[` / `]` chord adjusts the *next* placement.\n- M7.10b — **Inner-radius gizmo for Star**\n  - In edit mode for a Star node: paint a small grip on one of\n    the inner vertices; drag changes `inner_r` (clamped to\n    `(0, outer_r)`).\n  - Sides-count keyboard chord while selected: `[` / `]`\n    decrement / increment `points` (≥3).\n  - Gizmo paints through the OBB pipeline so it rotates\n    with the shape.\n- M7.10c — **Rounded-rect corner-radius dragger**\n  - In edit mode for a RoundedRect: small grip inset from one\n    corner. Drag along the diagonal scales `radius` (clamped\n    `[0, min(width, height) / 2]`).\n  - Single-handle (not per-corner) since the data variant is\n    `radius: f32`. Per-corner radius lives behind a\n    `CornerRadius` rewrite — defer to a follow-up.\n\nDependencies: none. Ships behind the existing FSM + gizmo\npaint stack.\n\nPen tool is currently click-anchors-only; the canonical Bézier\npen lets you drag from a placement to author handle tangents\nin one gesture.\n\n- M6.1 — **Pen tool drag-out Bézier handles**\n  - On `PointerDown` while placing an anchor, hold + drag\n    paints a CubicTo's `control2` (and the next segment's\n    `control1` mirrored). Release commits the anchor +\n    handles.\n  - FSM additions: `Drawing { Placing { anchor, last_handle:\n    Option\u003c(f32, f32)\u003e } }`.\n  - Rubber-band preview shows the would-be cubic from the\n    previous anchor.\n- M6.2 — **Free-hand / pencil tool**\n  - New `PencilTool` — captures `PointerMove` samples while\n    held; commits a `ShapePath::Path { commands: Vec\u003cLineTo\u003e }`\n    on release.\n  - Optional Ramer-Douglas-Peucker simplification at commit\n    (epsilon = `2.0` content units; share helper with M7.4f).\n  - Toolbar chip in a new or extended demo.\n- M6.3 — **Path simplify / fit-to-curve**\n  - `Action::PathSimplify` (Cmd+Alt+S) — runs RDP +\n    Schneider's curve-fit on the active path; commits via\n    `SetShapeCommand` so the result is undoable.\n  - Threshold knob lives on the action; default tuned for\n    pencil output.\n\nDependencies: M6.1 needs FSM tweaks but no Blinc work. M6.2 is\nself-contained. M6.3 reuses the M7.4f offset/simplify\ninfrastructure.\n\nVisual-property gizmos that operate directly on the OBB instead\nof through the (deferred) inspector panel. Data structures all\nexist; this is purely paint + drag math.\n\n- M7.11a — **Linear gradient gizmo**\n  - When the selection's fill is `Gradient::Linear`: paint a\n    line from gradient start → end with stop chips along it.\n  - Drag end-points → updates `start` / `end`. Drag a chip →\n    updates that stop's `t` (clamped `[0, 1]`).\n  - Double-click on the line between chips = insert stop at\n    that `t`. Right-click chip = delete.\n- M7.11b — **Radial gradient focus / radius grips**\n  - Centre handle = focus, ring handle = radius. Same chip\n    UX for stops along a radial axis.\n- M7.11c — **Stroke-width dragger**\n  - Side-edge handle that scales with the OBB; drag offsets\n    the stroke width (`stroke_width: f32` on the fill /\n    stroke struct). Live preview through `SetStrokeCommand`\n    or equivalent.\n- M7.11d — **Dash-array editor**\n  - Inline chips for each `dash`/`gap` length in the dash\n    pattern; drag a chip = scale that length. `+` chord adds\n    a `dash`/`gap` pair, `-` removes the trailing pair.\n  - May need a Blinc shader confirmation for arbitrary dash\n    arrays — check before scoping.\n- M7.11e — **Effect gizmos for shadow / blur / glow**\n  - Shadow: drag the offset vector; an inner ring scales blur\n    radius. Live updates through `SetEffectsCommand`.\n  - Blur: ring around the OBB; drag = `radius`.\n  - Glow: same as shadow without the offset; drag the ring.\n  - All three respect the M7.7 ephemeral mirror.\n\nDependencies: M7.11d may need Blinc shader work — confirm by\ninspecting `blinc_core::Stroke` / shader path before\ncommitting scope.\n\nFinal transform-tooling polish — pivot dragger + dedicated\nskew gizmo. Both unblock keyboard nudge by giving a direct\nmanipulation alternative.\n\n- M7.12a — **Pivot-point dragger**\n  - In transform mode: paint a small target glyph at the\n    OBB's pivot point. Drag → moves the pivot in local space.\n  - Reproject existing `translation` so the world position\n    of the shape stays fixed (similar to M7.2's\n    `recenter_translation`).\n  - Pivot persists on the node (new `Transform2D.pivot:\n    [f32; 2]`, defaults to `[0, 0]` = OBB centre).\n- M7.12b — **Dedicated skew gizmo handles**\n  - Two small handles outside the OBB on the `ResizeE` /\n    `ResizeS` axes. Drag tangent to the OBB edge → updates\n    `Transform2D.skew[0]` / `skew[1]`.\n  - Avoids the Blinc macOS modifier-flag gap (no Alt/Cmd\n    needed). Keyboard nudge (M7.5b) stays.\n\nDependencies: M7.12a needs a `Transform2D.pivot` field +\nserde plumbing. M7.12b is pure paint + math.\n\nGeometry composition operations that round out path\nauthoring. Clip-mask is the largest single piece of UX work\nin this plan.\n\n- M7.13a — **Vector clip-mask**\n  - `NodeKind::ClipMask` (or `Node.clip_mask: Option\u003cNodeId\u003e`\n    field) — the mask node clips siblings or the parent.\n  - `Action::ClipMaskWithSelection` — top selection becomes\n    the clip; remaining selection becomes the clipped subtree.\n  - Renderer: `paint_subtree` wraps clipped children in\n    `push_layer(LayerConfig { clip_path: ..., .. })`; mask\n    flattens through the existing `to_path_commands` helper.\n  - May need Blinc upstream confirmation for layer-clip via\n    a `ShapePath` rather than the existing CSS `clip_path`.\n- M7.13b — **Curve-preserving boolean ops**\n  - Replace M7's polyline-output booleans with cubic-aware\n    ops via lyon's path-bool or a hand-rolled Bentley-Ottmann\n    over cubics.\n  - Same `Action::Boolean*` chords; output preserves curves\n    when both operands are curve-only.\n- M7.13c — **Path offset (stroke → outlined fill)**\n  - `Action::PathOffsetToOutline` — converts a stroked path\n    to a filled outline (offset-out + offset-in unioned).\n  - Reuses M7.4f's polyline offset; cubic-aware when M7.13b\n    lands.\n\nDependencies: M7.13b is the longest item — reserve a\ngenerous slice. M7.13c reads as a wrapper around M7.13b once\nthat exists.\n\nLast polish layer — visual feedback for active tool + edit\nstate. Each is a small commit but lifts the editor's\ndiscoverability.\n\n- M7.14a — **Toolbar active-mode highlight**\n  - Each toolbar chip subscribes to the FSM store; chip\n    background reflects `mode_label`. Chip for the active\n    tool gets the accent stroke.\n  - Was deferred from M7.1; brings the toolbar in line with\n    the FSM's source-of-truth.\n- M7.14b — **Edit-mode visual indicator**\n  - Coloured outline strip across the top of the canvas\n    while in `EditingPath` state; subtitle shows the current\n    sub-state (\"editing path · subpath 0 · 4 anchors\").\n  - Subscribes to the FSM store + `EditorContextData`.\n\nDependencies: both lean on the existing FSM store + Blinc\nreactive primitives. No new infra.\n\n\n- **Snap to neighbouring anchors / 45° / perp** — M11 (snap\n  framework). Reuses the grid-snap scaffold; not tied to a\n  specific phase here.\n- **Align + distribute** — M11.\n- **Smart guides** — M11.\n- **Inspector panel for effects / fills / strokes / skew /\n  shape props** — M21 (editor shell). Inspectors land with\n  the rest of the panel system; on-canvas gizmos cover the\n  daily flow.\n- **3D SDF + CSG authoring** — blocked on Blinc upstream\n  (`DrawContext::push_sdf_shader`, `ruffle_sdf_codegen`,\n  `reflow_rt::components::gpu::sdf::live_render`). Track via\n  M17 readiness, not this plan.\n- **MaskImage layer effect** — Blinc supports it; deferred\n  until inspector ships (M21).\n- **Per-corner radius for RoundedRect** — needs a\n  `CornerRadius` data rewrite; out of scope for M7.10c's\n  uniform-radius dragger.\n\n\n- **P1 + P2 are independent** — could ship in parallel if\n  someone wants to pair on pen + pencil while another lands\n  the SDF tool family.\n- **P3 partially blocks on data confirmations** — gradient\n  fill struct, dash array storage, effect mutation ops; spike\n  one item before scoping the rest.\n- **P5 is the longest stretch** — clip-mask is a renderer\n  surface, curve booleans is a numeric stretch. Leave a buffer\n  for upstream Blinc PRs if `push_layer` doesn't take a\n  ShapePath today.\n- **P6 is opportunistic** — slot in between heavier phases as\n  a palette cleanser; doesn't need its own milestone window.\n\n\nPer the standing rule (every shipped feature gets a runnable\ndemo): each phase either extends an existing `m7_*` demo or\ncreates a new `m7.NN_*` example. Phase 1 extends `m7_sdf_tool`\nand `m8_subpath_edit`. Phase 2 likely needs `m6_pen_handles` +\n`m6_pencil`. Phase 3 needs `m7_gradient_gizmo` and\n`m7_effect_gizmos`. Phase 4 reuses `m7_2_gizmos`. Phase 5\nneeds `m7_clip_mask` + extends the existing booleans demo.\nPhase 6 ships a chip update inside `m7_sdf_tool`.","files":null}]}